>

  <h2>Why Daily 7 Exercises?</h2>
  <p>Consistency trumps intensity for long-term fitness. These seven exercises hit every major movement pattern using only your body weight, making them sustainable for life. Each takes seconds to perform but collectively build strength, mobility, and cardiovascular health.</p>

  <div class="not-prose">
    <div class="card my-6 bg-brand/5 p-5">
      <strong class="text-ink">Time Commitment:</strong>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body">Total time: 10-15 minutes. Can be split throughout the day.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>The 7 Daily Exercises</h2>

  <h3>1. March in Place (1 minute)</h3>
  <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Joint mobility, circulation, warm-up</p>
  <p><strong>How:</strong> Lift knees to hip height, swing arms naturally</p>

  <h3>2. Bodyweight Squats (1 minute, 10-15 reps)</h3>
  <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Legs, glutes, core, hip mobility</p>
  <p><strong>How:</strong> Feet shoulder-width, sit back like chair, drive through heels</p>
  <p><strong>Modification:</strong> Squat to chair, hold at bottom</p>

  <h3>3. Push-Ups (1 minute, 5-10 reps)</h3>
  <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Chest, shoulders, triceps, core</p>
  <p><strong>How:</strong> Hands under shoulders, body straight, lower chest to floor</p>
  <p><strong>Modification:</strong> Incline on wall or table</p>

  <h3>4. Glute Bridges (1 minute, 15-20 reps)</h3>
  <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Glutes, hamstrings, core, lower back</p>
  <p><strong>How:</strong> Lie on back, feet flat, lift hips squeezing glutes at top</p>
  <p><strong>Modification:</strong> Single-leg if standard is easy</p>

  <h3>5. Plank (1 minute, 30-60 seconds)</h3>
  <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Core strength, shoulders, posture</p>
  <p><strong>How:</strong> Forearms and toes on floor, body straight from head to heels</p>
  <p><strong>Modification:</strong> Drop to knees for support</p>

  <h3>6. Lunges (1 minute, 10 each leg)</h3>
  <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Legs, balance, hip mobility</p>
  <p><strong>How:</strong> Step forward, lower until both knees at 90 degrees</p>
  <p><strong>Modification:</strong> Use wall for balance, shorter steps</p>

  <h3>7. Jumping Jacks (1 minute, steady pace)</h3>
  <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Cardiovascular, coordination, full-body activation</p>
  <p><strong>How:</strong> Jump while raising arms and separating legs</p>
  <p><strong>Modification:</strong> Step jacks (no jumping) for joint-friendly option</p>

